# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF on every platform. Without this, a
# Windows clone with the Git default core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into
# RUN_CODEX_REVIEW.sh and bash refuses to run it:
#   RUN_CODEX_REVIEW.sh: line 13: $'\r': command not found
#   set: pipefail: invalid option name
# That breaks the review runner under Git Bash and WSL. Found by executing the
# runner in an autocrlf=true clone, not by inspection.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is fine with either, but keep Windows tooling conventional.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
